# std/agent-harvest (design/caos-expr.md): an entry for an OPERATION OF THE STEP. `@op` says llm-step
# does the work in process (it owns the conversation's own records and the call's
# lifecycle), so this entry exists to give the operation a path, a help and a place in
# `tool_help`/`run_tool`. The image it curries is never run.
HELP=<<END
Apply selected content changes from a terminal child using the same atomic reconciliation as file tools. Code, memories, and notes keep their conversation-relative paths; protocol metadata is excluded.
@param child The terminal child id agent-spawn returned.
@param {array} [paths] Paths to apply, including descendants. Omit for all changed content. Select code references as whole source trees.
@op agent-harvest
END
curry --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/llm-step --help=$HELP
